-- ProfileIntent — a sales intent. What to sell to a profile (item or
-- plan, optionally with a free-form note). Three EntityRef fields: one
-- bare (`profileId`) and two inside Maybe (`itemId`, `planId`).
--
-- Static rows: none. Identity (label / description / icon) is
-- registered by defineSystemEntity on the TS side.
--
-- Phase 3c of the system-entities sweep — see
-- workstreams/ts-elimination/briefs/phase-3c-profile-relations.md.
-- First .fenel to exercise `Maybe (EntityRef<"<name>">)` at field-
-- position — parens force `parseTypeAppArg`'s paren branch into full
-- `parseTypeExpr` recursion so the EntityRef shorthand inside resolves
-- correctly (without parens, `Maybe EntityRef<"item">` would parse as
-- `Maybe(EntityRef)` with leftover `<...>` tokens). All three EntityRef
-- field labels are overridden — humanize "Profile Id" / "Item Id" /
-- "Plan Id" mis-describe the entity-reference fields; the TS-side
-- `fieldLabels` block on defineSystemEntity renames them to "Profile",
-- "Item", "Plan" (the "drop the Id suffix" convention).

@entity
@codeName "profile_intent"
@label "Profile Intent"
@description "A sales intent — what to sell to a profile"
@icon "target"
@fieldLabel "profileId" "Profile"
@fieldLabel "itemId" "Item"
@fieldLabel "planId" "Plan"
ProfileIntent = ProfileIntent profileId: EntityRef<"profile"> itemId: Maybe (EntityRef<"item">) planId: Maybe (EntityRef<"plan">) note: Maybe String
